# Perplexity Multi-Vector Scout (`perplexity-multi-vector-scout`)

Brings Perplexity Pro and Sonar Deep Research multi-vector query decomposition into Claude Code.

## Core Capabilities
- **Orthogonal Query Decomposition:** Decomposes difficult technical questions into 4 targeted search vectors rather than running a single blunt search.
- **Cross-Source Grounding:** Synthesizes upstream documentation, closed GitHub pull requests, real-time commits, and package changelogs into a single evidence ledger.
- **Subagent Parallel Dispatch:** Feeds decomposed vectors to background subagents or web tools to retrieve data 4x faster.

## CLI Usage (`perplexity-scout`)
```bash
perplexity-scout "OGSR 64-bit sound distance attenuation GSC comment chunk"
```

## Interoperability
- Connects with `deep-research-synthesizer` to synthesize publication-grade technical findings.
- Connects with `grok-realtime-telemetry-scout` to search active commit logs for undocumented bug fixes.

## Windows 10/11 & Cross-Platform Parity (`windows-linux-cross-os-runtime-bridge`)
- Compatible with both Linux and Windows 10/11 (`install.ps1` / `.cmd` shims, `Path(tempfile.gettempdir())`, and native toolchain resolution).
